# Homelab infrastructure: current picture

Reviewed standing context, loaded into every session; deployed read-only
from `docker/openclaw/workspace/infra/TOOLS.md` (code-owned by @root).
Generated by `python3 ci/facts/render.py`: prose from `TOOLS.md.in`, the
parts marked *(from ...)* from the files named; CI fails when it is stale, so
fix a fact at its source, in an MR. If the repo or the live system disagrees
with this file, they win: say so.

## Hosts *(from ansible/inventory.yml)*

<!-- generated: hosts -->
- router: Ubuntu 24.04; routes every VLAN. Container data under
  `/persistent_data/application/`. Host services: telegraf, NUT, restic,
  tailscaled, the GitLab runners. Pis: Debian 12 (zwave also has the miniDSP
  units and snapclient; satellite-2 the scanner; kernel and bootloader
  follow-ups still in progress). macmini: iMessage bridge.
- Off-box: healthchecks.io dead-man check, restic offsite repo (B2).

## Network (details: docs/NETWORK.md, docs/FIREWALL.md)

<!-- generated: vlans -->
- external: internet-facing, behind nginx. internal: lab services, GitLab,
  Vault, OpenClaw. mgmt: switches, APs, IPMI, UPS. iot: Home Assistant, MQTT,
  Zigbee, Snapcast, AV. VLAN 7 reserved.
- Lab egress goes through Mullvad WireGuard (the only WireGuard; `wg0`/`wg1`
  are gone); remote access is Tailscale (subnet router). Vaultwarden, Audioserve and Home
  Assistant answer only to LAN and tailnet; Nextcloud, Plex, Ombi and the
  static blog are public. DNS: Pi-hole. NTP: the router (the S2500 syncs from it). Switch/AP config:
  `networking/`.

## Services *(from the compose files each host renders)*

<!-- generated: services -->
- Proxies: `nginx` (external), `lab_nginx`, `iot_nginx`. `docker-socket-proxy`
  serves CI image builds; `docker-socket-proxy-ro` (read-only) lets promtail
  discover containers. Service names: vaultwarden is `bitwarden`, audioserve
  `booksonic`, drawio `diagram`. deluge goes out through Mullvad; nextcloud
  runs on MariaDB 12.3 LTS.
- influxdb 2.9: bucket `metrics`, org `homelab`; tokens are stored hashed, so
  one can't be read back later, only recreated. telegraf is a host service on
  the router and a container on the Pis.
- **Gone; don't reference or recreate them:** the whole voice stack
  (Rhasspy, Hermes, satellites' voice services), WordPress (the blog is
  static), clawrouter, Portainer.

